# Documentation only: this file is never loaded. Put real settings in .env (git-ignored) or the environment.
# The values shown are the defaults in makeConfig() (src/config.ts).
PORT=3480
# The server binds to 127.0.0.1 unless HOST says otherwise.
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# The Calendly-style webhook is signed. With no key the door answers 503. `npm run dev` and `npm run replay`
# set this one inline for the local demo; it is not a secret:
# CALENDLY_SIGNING_KEY=local-demo-signing-key-not-a-secret
# The cockpit's send-a-lead form and Replay a day (/api/demo/*) answer 404 unless this is 1. `npm run dev` sets it.
# DEMO_ROUTES=1
# LLM: ollama (default) | rules (no model) | anthropic (disabled unless the key below is also set)
LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2:3b
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# The model runs before routing only when its answer can change the route; other free-text leads get it after the alert
# (docs/DECISIONS.md #19). "all" puts it before every free-text route, as before. Leads preparing at once, model calls at once:
# MODEL_BEFORE_ROUTE=gated
# PREPARE_CONCURRENCY=4
# MODEL_CONCURRENCY=1
# The outbound module's rate file (npm run rates:fetch puts Serif's public export here) and its hand-made platform mapping
# (docs/DECISIONS.md #20). Loaded at startup when either changes.
# RATES_CSV=data/rates/mrf_rate_search_export.csv
# OUTBOUND_PLATFORMS=fixtures/outbound-platforms.json
# The synthetic usage fixtures (features, deals, PostHog-shaped events; docs/DECISIONS.md #22). Loaded at startup when they change.
# USAGE_FIXTURES=fixtures/usage
# HubSpot is dry-run unless BOTH are set. Service keys replaced private apps, which HubSpot
# stopped allowing on Oct 26, 2026 (a legacy HUBSPOT_PRIVATE_APP_TOKEN still works).
# HUBSPOT_SERVICE_KEY=
# HUBSPOT_LIVE=1
